       "Dolly visits the dentist with a troublesome tooth and wants it extracted.",
       "The dentist pulls out her tooth and says it is his first tooth — Dolly is shocked, thinking he has started practising on her; but he clarifies that she is his first patient in his private practice.",
       "He asks why she refused gas (anaesthesia); she says it would have cost five shillings extra. He regrets hurting her for five shillings; she replies that hurting people is his job.",
       "The dentist set up his clinic only six weeks ago; the premises are on rent, the furniture belongs to the landlord, and the professional equipment is on hire-purchase.",
       "He is a bachelor; his family does not live with him.",
       "He is called the 'five-shilling dentist' because he charges five shillings for each thing.",
       "Dolly gives him a brand-new five-shilling piece as his first fee and tells him to drill a hole in it and wear it on his watch-chain — an ironical remark.",
